    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. it's a solid start but i'm a bit worried. it feels a little... polished? maybe a bit too much like a template. \n\nthe board is actually really picky about the \"impact\" section. specifically, they want to see more depth on the long-term survival of the systems. if i run this through the screening tool, it gets a score of 5. that's okay, but if we're going to win this grant against the other NGOs, we probably need a higher density of those core impact concepts to ensure it passes the initial filter without getting flagged as \"low impact.\"\n\ncan you refine this? try to deepen the narrative about the villages, but make sure the connection to those themes (sustainability, resilience, etc.) is even more explicit. just please, keep it sounding like a person wrote it. i don't want it to look like you just copy-pasted a list of keywords.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
